WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.870
Step on a pin, and a message
races along your nerves as an

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.990
electrical impulse, in a split second.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.010
But your body also sends messages
a slower way: as chemicals,

4
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.470
carried along in your blood.

5
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.170
These can take far longer to arrive.

6
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.530
So why would your body ever
bother with the slow route?

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.610
In this mission, you'll compare
the nervous system with the

8
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.650
endocrine system.

9
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.650
You'll meet hormones:

10
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.750
chemicals made by glands and
carried in the blood to target

11
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.770
organs.

12
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.510
And you'll weigh up speed against
how long each kind of message

13
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.870
lasts.

14
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.890
Your mission: explain why your
body uses a slow messenger as

15
00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.500
well as a fast one.
